    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n614" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">actĭto</span></b> , āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq.</i> [ago], <i>to act</i> or <i>be employed in</i>,
				<i>often</i> or <i>much</i> (only of
				judicial or dramatic action): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multas privatas causas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 70</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tragoedias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rep. 4, 35</span></i>
			: so <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Galb. 3</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Gell. 9, 6</span></i>.</div>
